constant term.\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $5.$ However, it also contains a term ($2{x}^{3}y$) that is of degree $4.$ Therefore, not all of its terms are of degree $5.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ and all of its terms are of degree $3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115222 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80449399-3ae4-593f-8c3b-00bcdcc99727" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Outside of the Range of Cosecant" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048533 :topic/id #uuid "a7996653-9e76-59d9-b493-05cb731632cb" :topic/math-academy-id 1566 :topic/title "Elementary Trigonometric Equations Containing Cosecant"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "813d5f30-9e48-5a6a-b6e6-2bb8fba1d9b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473212} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b647d2-7171-5fbc-aa5a-c488c8e93a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7b647d2-7171-5fbc-aa5a-c488c8e93a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473213} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e6082c7-bc86-5235-bb42-ac7ce8892f29" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed140b0d-d3db-5c2d-ac0b-434ba7495455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473214} {:answer/id #uuid "fe733efc-71ed-5232-84aa-79a588a2cd3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value 