t the range of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation I has no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115222 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80449399-3ae4-593f-8c3b-00bcdcc99727" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Outside of the Range of Cosecant" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048533 :topic/id #uuid "a7996653-9e76-59d9-b493-05cb731632cb" :topic/math-academy-id 1566 :topic/title "Elementary Trigonometric Equations Containing Cosecant"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aeca81e-f826-54fb-8582-a310163753dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473368} {:answer/id #uuid "d375d389-1cc5-564d-9008-f339acf0faf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d375d389-1cc5-564d-9008-f339acf0faf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473369} :answer-field/id #uuid "f930cda1-ffab-5ac5-bd75-4fd94bf83142" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ca3a4d6-75ee-5373-be8c-c30e6c467982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473370} {:answer/id #uuid "efb69d5c-8fcb-5779-9057-cf2ecdf4012b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473371}] :a