ext} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453884} :answer-field/id #uuid "81040326-5134-5a42-8539-aac88ecd9a5e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a907de-0404-5ffb-8362-e9676298070b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36139" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{3}$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$\n- **II.** The limit evaluates to $-1$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2}$\n- **III.** The limit exists and is equal to $\\frac{1}{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+2\\cdot 0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=-{x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2(-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048449 :topic/id #uuid "a05758d1-f2b4-5a86-b7b0-c2a4bb6dcb85" :topic/math-academy-id 1931 :topic/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions"} :activity/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407821} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407852}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e09de5d-566b-53b7-938e-4cd69784f908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453162} {:answer/id #uuid "09739bfe-5ef1-5a91-a5aa-5281c92dda9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e09de5d-566b-53b7-938e-4cd69784f908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453162} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d5a350-84ff-5946-86f2-1d19d8d7220c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cee3daa-3190-55b4-a76d-c60b5757491d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453164} {:answer/id #uuid "f84f942c-6e9f-5b7c-af7b-f2c81298fce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f84f942c-6e9f-5b7c-af7b-f2c81298fce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453165} :answer-field/id #uuid "631b3c6b-1149-5d42-a891-5e829966c88f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53fda273-36a0-5e47-98ef-2cc2874bb65a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453166} {:answer/id #uuid "747834de-2a79-5887-b0c3-1e01bf258a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "747834de-2a79-5887-b0c3-1e01bf258a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453167} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae9ece0-8770-5aea-a183-8518985dc8d5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a3dbd42-cd16-5083-8842-33f0028feb3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105207" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,4]\\to [-3,9]$ which is given by $f(x)=2x+1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(-2)=f(4)$\n- **II.** $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- **III.** $f$ is an injection" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/5f/5fd931a87d6a5fb32d10ed931f443a8175f0760eba9fe2fe69336f8f79e9fd68.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have $f(2)=2(-2)+1=-3$ and $f(4)=2\\cdot 4+1=9.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $[-2,4]$ that map to the same element in $[-3,9].$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"} :activity/title "Injections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407855} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407892}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f45ad8ed-5b6d-5e46-b337-02ab271013b3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections From Functions Given Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d35f4e88-6bef-5641-80a0-028f685e3519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472466} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3f2a4a-cd53-59d2-a981-e675cff4a3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd3f2a4a-cd53-59d2-a981-e675cff4a3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472467} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0534f15-2962-5ddb-8f73-7a2f2475c0f6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473628} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19b312ff-ce3e-5e32-9aeb-756e89a5f671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472468} {:answer/id #uuid "258df532-e4f2-5710-b640-abc2180b4c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19b312ff-ce3e-5e32-9aeb-756e89a5f671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472468} :answer-field/id #uuid "29f20d63-79e9-56ff-8e1e-a8b4a6fa0751" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473629} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dc08267-7ffc-5f21-aad1-afa99e374adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472470} {:answer/id #uuid "b144395e-d1f5-57f9-9d59-546422f9a22d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dc08267-7ffc-5f21-aad1-afa99e374adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472470} :answer-field/id #uuid "09886aba-2044-5edb-a629-02c3209ba59e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23e55f80-c083-57f4-820d-7aa2d67256ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-105210" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n- **I.** $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=2x+3$\n- **II.** $g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=(x-2)^{2}$\n- **III.** $h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- I is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3 & =2{x}_{2}+3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- II is *not*  an injection.  For example, $g(1)=1=g(3),$ but $1\\ne 3.$\n\n- III is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(2\\pi ),$ but $0\\ne 2\\pi .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"} :activity/title "Injections" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407855} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407894}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals" :topic/_kn