question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b46ac655-a97e-50cb-a022-2af841ed15e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160451" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{7}}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a264b855-1904-5164-bede-a3a58bf8a87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473344} {:answer/id #uuid "76849f48-b02a-51c8-ab54-bc3cea4dc51e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76849f48-b02a-51c8-ab54-bc3cea4dc51e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473345} :answer-field/id #uuid "65d6b9db-5cf9-5d84-a615-3117e641ebb8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96047d36-a564-5410-a080-0f5ee960c506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473346} {:answer/id #uuid "21ca83ec-352e-5cd0-8ac7-bbcc21f9368c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96047d36-a564-5410-a080-0f5ee960c506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473346} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e78b1e-a0f9-5ef4-8159-54dc686fe017" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "577ef78e-2229-5fcf-aacf-90f73efb2e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473348} {:answer/id #uuid "9895344f-eccd-5c07-97f0-80c877ad5005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9895344f-eccd-5c07-97f0-80c877ad5005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473349} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fa22280-2abd-5607-b207-841f7d4a254b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ce0c9ed-8f49-5909-b44d-93bd60aa3e7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76964" :question/problem "Given that $26≡8\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=9$\n- **II.** $n=8$\n- **III.** $n=3$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=26-8=18.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $9∣18$ because $18÷9=2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\n- Note that $8∤18.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=8.$\n\n- Note that $3∣18$ because $18÷3=6,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409433 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e3b57aa-3f05-58d8-8630-4c61e4a9f20a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472448} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b42f5c-a47b-5d87-955d-4192d359f4e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/iden