{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c433443-9a9c-5d0b-84b5-bc247b100915" :question/math-academy-id "q-103390" :question/problem "Given that $29≡-16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=5$\n- **II.** $n=8$\n- **III.** $n=9$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=29-(-16)=45.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $5∣45$ because $45÷5=9,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=5.$\n\n- Note that $8∤45.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=8.$\n\n- Note that $9∣45$ because $45÷9=5,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "398716c2-d0e6-5106-a702-2f71d957726f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Integers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d490cf1-d662-56a2-8631-21d543f11c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453120} {:answer/id #uuid "ce480cda-9021-5f06-a8cd-b9ca16301c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d490cf1-d662-56a2-8631-21d543f11c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453120} :answer-field/id #uuid "af1230fc-88f6-56f0-a44f-a2580bb43a87" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5f14a7e-4460-5c56-88cd-b67e7eb770b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453122} {:answer/id #uuid "168ce81c-a8ca-550c-ae67-a01761495d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5f14a7e-4460-5c56-88cd-b67e7eb770b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453122} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b1c902-2a3c-5a5a-8275-9ced53169a21" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454311} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9917c881-2ee9-5be2-b248-f90217ecd423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453124} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a8e630-8f3b-5355-ac11-368a8e967b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8a8e630-8f3b-5355-ac11-368a8e967b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453125} :answer-field/id #uuid "0490fa62-dcfa-5271-a176-054c103e687c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a4a4ae5-eba9-597a-b12c-2ce503fbc86a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103385" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $11≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- **II.** $18≡16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- **III.** $24≡19\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Case I gives a false statement because $3∤(11-3).$ Notice that $11-3=8,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Case II gives a false statement because $4∤(18-16).$ Notice that $18-16=2,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\n- Case III gives a true statement. Indeed, $5∣(24-19).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(24-19)÷5=5÷5=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6939e2c-5e4c-5d3c-b411-121e989019d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453964} {:answer/id #uuid "42527d1d-51eb-5aa0-b849-c3505c852646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6939e2c-5e4c-5d3c-b411-121e989019d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453964} :answer-field/id #uuid "c65be09a-f53c-5c58-909a-d975c0b29817" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454732} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbaf0ed3-4c76-557d-bc51-6406555d6dc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453966} {:answer/id #uuid "c93051af-e99c-5c12-a773-dfc66b74d11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbaf0ed3-4c76-557d-bc51-6406555d6dc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453966} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8d44745-35ed-5099-bb46-c9a6bdbcf88a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454733} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e654702c-0d8c-5636-9f91-64969cdd47b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453968} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d41efc-3f6b-5285-a299-04b9702a043c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6d41efc-3f6b-5285-a299-04b9702a043c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453969} :answer-field/id #uuid "7387b7e6-f6df-542e-b959-1cad4caa776a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42227076-6750-5c0c-9261-152604f91699" :question/math-academy-id "q-76953" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $17≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$\n- **II.** $23≡-10\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$\n- **III.** $33≡12\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false because $9∤(17-2).$ Notice that $17-2=15,$ which is not divisible by $9.$\n\n- Statement II is false because $5∤(23-(-10)).$ Notice that $23-(-10)=33,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\n- Statement III is true because $7\\,|\\,(33-12).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(33-12)÷7=21÷7=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3016bf9-ac07-568b-b859-192d9dfd33ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473350} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5e8f2d-7445-500e-b3e5-a3eb69715f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e5e8f2d-7445-500e-b3e5-a3eb69715f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473351} :answer-field/id #uuid "8483680e-a732-595e-9351-f699605b91e7" :answer-fie