 the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=3$\n- **II.** $n=4$\n- **III.** $n=5$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=8-23=-15.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $3∣(-15)$ because $(-15)÷3=-5,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=3.$\n\n- Note that $4∤(-15).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=4.$\n\n- Note that $5∣(-15)$ because $(-15)÷5=-3,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409438 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f04d70d-73a1-5162-9f13-8c681e7e193a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472454} {:answer/id #uuid "efc94db3-7067-59e2-b764-6e84247a288b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efc94db3-7067-59e2-b764-6e84247a288b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472455} :answer-field/id #uuid "c66a189f-578d-55e4-bdc2-1726630fe3a1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473622} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec5cfca5-57a8-5d17-8eef-2d6f69737e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472456} {:answer/id #uuid "0c2806a1-0cf2-551c-839f-c0c7f5e0fc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c2806a1-0cf2-551c-839f-c0c7f5e0fc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472457} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb3a4ff-595a-555b-9da8-7e75ffc712e8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58ccace3-f408-56e1-9c02-05d74458e048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472458} {:answer/id #uuid "78380acd-858f-5c58-82d8-b81a2480ef87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78380acd-858f-5c58-82d8-b81a2480ef87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472459} :answer-field/id #uuid "86b77862-b26a-5bc0-b724-f4958124abbb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a58d29a-b4cc-50fc-9d69-711422d71682" :question/math-academy-id "q-103490" :question/problem "Given that $13≡-5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$, which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=3$\n- **II.** $n=6$\n- **III.** $n=9$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=13-(-5)=18.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $3∣18$ because $18÷3=6,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=3.$\n\n- Note that $6∣18$ because $18÷6=3,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=6.$\n\n- Note that $9∣18$ because $18÷9=2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2325c00a-6377-5d3f-8e31-1a81805e5899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453970} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6dd81c-8cb5-59f5-a508-2111c88efa9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c6dd81c-8cb5-59f5-a508-2111c88efa9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453971} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b371275-6d7b-5b97-8c3b-4bd36ec051e3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454735} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2d67da-1615-5493-bc76-35012297de9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453972} {:answer/id #uuid "18ef6a60-8030-55f2-9da0-921283250a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a2d67da-1615-5493-bc76-35012297de9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453972} :answer-field/id #uuid "6252a9b3-c085-5ff6-bf8e-08227b893b43" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c1e360a-6eaa-5672-b5fd-0ff6e047a87c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453974} {:answer/id #uuid "41922cf8-75b9-562c-8d22-97b501963686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41922cf8-75b9-562c-8d22-97b501963686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453975} :answer-field/id #uuid "3486679b-149d-5c68-b66e-923ed8ccc572" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae89ee49-3f2d-51e4-a2f6-ac3e918a674e" :question/math-academy-id "q-76958" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $12≡36\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$\n- **II.** $-9≡18\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- **III.** $21≡45\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true because $2∣(12-36).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(12-36)÷2=-24÷2=-12\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false because $4∤(-9-18).$ Notice that $-9-18=-27,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\n- Statement III is true because $8\\,|\\,(21-45).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(21-45)÷8=-24÷8=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f096c075-5b46-5ce6-a234-377c581a476b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453976} {:answer/id #uuid "6863ca49-960a-5d77-9a3a-7d0d0aa1dd85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f096c075-5b46-5ce6-a234-377c581a476b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453976} :answer-field/id #uuid "e94e7c51-516a-5014-af78-5555d5511fb7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc0ffaae-5eca-57b7-a644-173f07d6b749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453978} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e3cde8-deea-59b4-8676-00eeb50e5aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0e3cde8-deea-59b4-8676-00eeb50e5aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453979} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cdc0adf-283c-5e72-a33c-9caf5b09e916" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454739} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4664ac9-65c6-53be-af21-37ab3cf61812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453980} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e95427-5a86-5e7d-9c59-7539f2ab125f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4664ac9-65c6-53be-af21-37ab3cf61812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453980} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb6cfb2-0eb7-58cd-885c-671d59601b18" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b17c24c5-e750-5126-8785-6318018ca783" :question/math-academy-id "q-76959" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-5≡11\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- **II.** $-7≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$\n- **III.** $6≡25\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false because $3∤(-5-11).$ Notice that $-5-11=-16,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Statement II is true because $7\\,|\\,(-7-0).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-7-0)÷7=-7÷7=-7\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false because $9∤(6-25).$ Notice that $6-25=-19,$ which is not divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42708017-2e08-541a-a0c3-70b49941a5a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472442} {:answer/id #uuid "e796520e-fbe7-52e2-88bd-0591456c7db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e796520e-fbe7-52e2-88bd-0591456c7db2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472443} :answer-field/id #uuid "88b8daba-48cf-53e7-bdcb-854ca7473f00" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473616} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2fcceb-6977-5edc-b972-6ef48acdf27f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472444} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a188cf-5a7a-50fd-aea8-3c7c08b142c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1a188cf-5a7a-50fd-aea8-3c7c08b142c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472445} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c6d071-eb27-5b7d-8267-405e1cf6365a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473617} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "686ee57d-c0d8-5367-a4e4-b83dca7772e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472446} {:answer/id #uuid "3a0a5473-9207-5805-87cb-d995d33d62f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a0a5473-9207-5805-87cb-d995d33d62f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472447} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a676e29-3d72-5aed-abaf-a3b3398036a5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e77d765e-3b79-5534-bec0-79f592cc8d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103387" :question/problem "Given that $-3≡15\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=2$\n- **II.** $n=6$\n- **III.** $n=9$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=-3-15=-18.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $2∣(-18)$ because $(-18)÷2=-9,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\n- Note that $6∣(-18)$ because $(-18)÷6=-3,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=6.$\n\n- Note that $9∣(-18)$ because $(-18)÷9=-2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2cb28a0-b456-55cc-94c3-2a35edde21be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Integers are Coprime" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048141 :topic/id #uuid "82ca0e31-666b-5e06-8d65-c724c2ffa4fb" :topic/math-academy-id 2676 :topic/title "The Euclidean Algorithm"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16764622-cd26-55e1-8a5a-7e55b57682c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454286} {:answer/id #uuid "ba98f67b-67c0-5060-a532-9100f74d628f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba98f67b-67c0-5060-a532-9100f74d628f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454287} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d2efd04-ce36-5615-b920-a167a18c5522" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83f64992-3a27-5317-b1d1-b10093213230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454288} {:answer/id #uuid "ede5a4d3-58f8-507f-ae2f-d2870f910272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83f64992-3a27-5317-b1d1-b10093213230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454288} :answer-field/id #uuid "71ae289e-e270-51af-ae40-76298154f43a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03a8cbab-7fe7-5051-b478-b3b6fcd97579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454290} {:answer/id #uuid "647bb829-b1ad-502f-ac68-5b6629e48201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03a8cbab-7fe7-5051-b478-b3b6fcd97579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454290} :answer-field/id #uuid "d885f16a-81d5-5090-9f2d-2ec0e5cb9bd6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3936dcf8-3c18-5d25-b1ef-fee251049b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-98480" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{gcd}(765,221)=17$\n- **II.** $\\text{gcd}(765,221)=1$\n- **III.** $765$ and $221$ are coprime" :question/worked-solution "Recall that two integers are coprime if their greatest common divisor is $1.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Indeed, let's use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}765 & = & 221\\cdot 3 & + & 102 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 221 & = & 102\\cdot 2 & + & 17 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 102 & = & 17\\cdot 6 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $17.$ So, the greatest common divisor of $765$ and $221$ is $17:$\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(765,221)=17.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\text{gcd}(765,221)>1,$ the numbers are not coprime.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2cb28a0-b456-55cc-94c3-2a35edde21be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Integers are Coprime" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048141 :topic/id #uuid "82ca0e31-666b-5e06-8d65-c724c2ffa4fb" :topic/math-academy-id 2676 :topic/title "The Euclidean Algorithm"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db731a1-a78b-5cb1-a275-94cbe9841b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454280} {:answer/id #uuid "20717d2e-b744-557d-ad03-8171eb0fe0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20717d2e-b744-557d-ad03-8171eb0fe0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454281} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e0f46f2-efa3-5704-b207-3ba4ba50b150" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc7102cd-274c-58e2-87f3-08c5cb93e7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454282} {:answer/id #uuid "b1de85d5-8373-5a85-b4e2-04e2966728e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc7102cd-274c-58e2-87f3-08c5cb93e7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454282} :answer-field/id #uuid "46d91d1b-2581-5b40-9708-ebfc3af5ab0d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454891} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45ce2b6b-04ba-54be-b4bd-44f2f525400b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454284} {:answer/id #uuid "bb42e7bc-6591-52cb-99cd-ccd37cce4d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb42e7bc-6591-52cb-99cd-ccd37cce4d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454285} :answer-field/id #uuid "81c1cd10-879f-568b-97d2-c3cefe49ca99" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e2b9768-6303-5aa7-8a02-db48065ae94a" :question/math-academy-id "q-98476" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{gcd}(5719,2669)=1$\n- **II.** $\\text{gcd}(5719,2669)=3$\n- **III.** $5719$ and $2669$ are coprime" :question/worked-solution "Recall that two integers are coprime if their greatest common divisor is $1.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Indeed, let's use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}5719 & = & 2669\\cdot 2 & + & 381 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 2669 & = & 381\\cdot 7 & + & 2 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 381 & = & 2\\cdot 190 & + & 1 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 2 & = & 1\\cdot 2 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $1.$ So, the greatest common divisor of $5719$ and $2669$ is $1:$\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(5719,2669)=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{gcd}(5719,2669)=1,$ the numbers are coprime.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e148fac7-727b-55d9-ba67-0a9fc7a276e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453368} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6ec723-5cd2-5173-b8f1-1778f583295d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c6ec723-5cd2-5173-b8f1-1778f583295d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453369} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e8e1392-18d1-56b3-b0f5-ff3dd861687a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454434} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a536093-cb71-5d44-a52f-8e05b4b9f74a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453370} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2d5ab2-a228-5241-aef5-decbffea282c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc2d5ab2-a228-5241-aef5-decbffea282c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453371} :answer-field/id #uuid "deacc4af-75f1-5a94-a0d0-5d1ad4ac3ea8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454435} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80b4f556-0cc0-5fc7-9fac-56ff9260d6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453372} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd91732-9818-5742-9c5d-ea668d6dbe0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbd91732-9818-5742-9c5d-ea668d6dbe0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453373} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f7af479-38a3-58de-bca6-c137a88e2790" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a3b6388-98bd-5083-8d1c-f60a05890b23" :question/math-academy-id "q-132726" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(\\sqrt{3},1)$\n- **II.** ${f}_{x}(1,\\sqrt{3})$ is defined\n- **III.** ${f}_{y}(0,1)$ is defined" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}+1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}+1}\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(\\sqrt{3},1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(\\sqrt{3},1)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1})=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nand both partial derivatives are also defined at $(\\sqrt{3},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\sqrt{3},1) & =\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {f}_{y}(\\sqrt{3},1) & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $f$ itself is defined at $(1,\\sqrt{3})$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,\\sqrt{3})=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{x}$ is also defined at $(1,\\sqrt{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is also true. Indeed, the function $f$ itself is defined at $(0,1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(0,1)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{0}{1})=0,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(0,1)=-\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"} :activity/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409538} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409564}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "899f43e4-fc9a-5506-b84d-a25c2d9eb6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453928} {:answer/id #uuid "ec4690b4-12f7-5ffd-a0f0-d137fa95703c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "899f43e4-fc9a-5506-b84d-a25c2d9eb6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453928} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ccf0ae7-dc64-51f0-892e-8d88c6910e82" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454714} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "376cf739-f8d8-5cb0-91a0-52b41ea250c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453930} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcc07c3-7704-591c-aebf-ff0249e9dd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffcc07c3-7704-591c-aebf-ff0249e9dd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453931} :answer-field/id #uuid "72f29120-e8c2-52fc-abd7-8386d5f878c4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc77c615-3280-58d4-a19d-18282a3f7486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453932} {:answer/id #uuid "8cfc9ce4-4706-5c6b-8f71-059b43d404d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc77c615-3280-58d4-a19d-18282a3f7486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453932} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c89136-ff34-5898-9f58-5a98f17bcfb1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "538fdcf0-8dcd-525c-becd-0317742dbf1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72010" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(1,-1)$\n\n- **II.** ${f}_{y}(-1,-1)$ is defined\n\n- **III.** ${f}_{x}(0,1)$ is defined" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\cdot \\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\cdot \\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2\\sqrt{xy}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one. \n\n- Statement I is false. If we substitute $(1,-1)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(1,-1)={e}^{\\sqrt{(1)(-1)}}=-{e}^{\\sqrt{-1}}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have a negative number under the radical.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(-1,-1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(-1,-1)={e}^{\\sqrt{(-1)(-1)}}={e}^{\\sqrt{1}}={e}^{1}=e,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(-1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-1,-1) & =\\frac{(-1){e}^{\\sqrt{(-1)(-1)}}}{2\\sqrt{(-1)(-1)}}=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1}}}{2\\sqrt{1}}=-\\frac{e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we substitute $(0,1)$ into ${f}_{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(0,1)=1\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{0\\cdot 1}}}{2\\sqrt{0\\cdot 1}}=\\frac{{e}^{0}}{2\\sqrt{0}}=\\frac{1}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II  only'." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"} :activity/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409538} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409560}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409584 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d56b033-a2c8-57c7-adde-e574d726ec78" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting Symbolic Conditional Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049805 :topic/id #uuid "155403ed-fbfa-59a9-b928-e762a73145ef" :topic/math-academy-id 247 :topic/title "Logical Equivalence with Conditional Statements"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d0f8fb4-d1b2-5bff-ba27-c6e4e679e31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453634} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7d44c8-3ad6-50d2-9658-d18a60e921c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e7d44c8-3ad6-50d2-9658-d18a60e921c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453635} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba7a927-c65d-53d2-a68e-2a711452828e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454567} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8c84692-3840-51b5-880d-3386d31c4f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453636} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc1d84f-0a08-51e1-9122-944928bd54c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dc1d84f-0a08-51e1-9122-944928bd54c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453637} :answer-field/id #uuid "91aa8150-4bc8-561c-9c32-8cfddb99b464" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454568} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f8ce0ad-e15d-5071-aae6-6ebf6f10905b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453638} {:answer/id #uuid "34bd4c0a-6891-5927-8f43-1900cd830078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f8ce0ad-e15d-5071-aae6-6ebf6f10905b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453638} :answer-field/id #uuid "728d40e4-2d8b-5727-be86-396f6263ab1f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1308109d-5efe-51ad-bfa1-4050522344dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-182506" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A⇒¬B≡¬(A∧B)$\n- **II.** $¬(A⇒¬B)≡A∧B$\n- **III.** $¬(A⇒¬B)≡¬A∧B$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $A⇒¬B$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬A∨¬B,$ which by De Morgan's law is equivalent to $¬(A∧B).$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. From part I, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\nA⇒¬B≡¬(A∧B)\n$$\n\nBy negating this statement, we get\n\n$$\n¬(A⇒¬B)≡¬(¬(A∧B)).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we reach\n\n$$\nA∧B.\n$$\n\nSo, $¬(A⇒¬B)$ is equivalent to $A∧B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049805 :topic/id #uuid "155403ed-fbfa-59a9-b928-e762a73145ef" :topic/math-academy-id 247 :topic/title "Logical Equivalence with Conditional Statements"} :activity/title "Logical Equivalence with Conditional Statements" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409565} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409587}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409610 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051085 :topic/id #uuid "7fdf89be-7454-5a23-9d34-17c62e869eea" :topic/math-academy-id 2132 :topic/title "The Curl of a Vector Field"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8286c6dd-7fea-5018-b722-69a0848b0bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437502} {:answer/id #uuid "5d52abdf-7ac5-55e3-92ae-9aec71a85bbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8286c6dd-7fea-5018-b722-69a0848b0bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437502} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb53bf33-5552-5395-8fd4-4d42b50a2a01" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4939bd9-e529-5af3-b533-59e09598d0e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437504} {:answer/id #uuid "2b9d89e5-98a9-5520-8de9-5ddb178c0664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b9d89e5-98a9-5520-8de9-5ddb178c0664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437505} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a596bab-34c8-5ee7-9e82-c47a2988e863" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "273314f4-9ed1-52ac-8d9b-6701a93d8748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437506} {:answer/id #uuid "265725b9-3d43-5f84-a380-552591b33792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "265725b9-3d43-5f84-a380-552591b33792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437507} :answer-field/id #uuid "05fd84cc-0dd3-5f03-9595-e86a0cb51c38" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438782} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fc09d16-5459-5df8-9d7e-c5304315ffbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437508} {:answer/id #uuid "3423417a-d67c-5bac-8ed6-720f61a5aa60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fc09d16-5459-5df8-9d7e-c5304315ffbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437508} :answer-field/id #uuid "31b1fd93-e1ee-539e-8481-cca67e61611b" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "656969c6-847a-533c-a9b8-d526f82e1ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105694" :question/problem "![](images/17/17637e938a25e91b9a03921dbbe0f22c8ea760f09cfed9b4a76d07bd5e3b9301.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction.\n- **IV.** $F$ is irrotational" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/f3/f385add60afac473a5734f8c1ed57c6575bada03c9c16b24fed73b200c38e2c5.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate clockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (clockwise), our thumb will point into the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points into the screen, in the direction of decreasing $z.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051085 :topic/id #uuid "7fdf89be-7454-5a23-9d34-17c62e869eea" :topic/math-academy-id 2132 :topic/title "The Curl of a Vector Field"} :activity/title "The Curl of a Vector Field" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409590} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409611}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048808 :topic/id #uuid "c1647abf-57b4-5851-a828-2952c6947148" :topic/math-academy-id 948 :topic/title "Indicator Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73398205-b447-5295-a67c-ad006a848004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453574} {:answer/id #uuid "66ac170a-d95d-5009-aef4-e8e0a5826587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66ac170a-d95d-5009-aef4-e8e0a5826587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453575} :answer-field/id #uuid "cabc922e-c483-5964-999a-afcbcd1b58ba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ebd81b-61aa-58e2-8fe6-1acf2a46536f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453576} {:answer/id #uuid "c16f5c20-ce58-58cc-a4b2-847c9c364e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10ebd81b-61aa-58e2-8fe6-1acf2a46536f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453576} :answer-field/id #uuid "0188fa47-67f0-516d-a06e-0f6db7d50605" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b9dc1f-cc8d-5093-ba46-67a90d725c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453578} {:answer/id #uuid "986b4a97-0064-5e3c-bb93-d96d0717fad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "986b4a97-0064-5e3c-bb93-d96d0717fad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453579} :answer-field/id #uuid "1683ca8d-d357-5b5b-a758-4c8420293a37" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09ca95e9-e7fd-5d14-80c3-ab64bc50a23d" :question/math-academy-id "q-174385" :question/problem "Given that ${1}_{A}(q)=0,$ which of the following statements about $\\overset{―}{A}$ are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=0$\n\n- **III.** $q\\in \\overset{―}{A}$\n\n*Hint: ${1}_{A}$ denotes the indicator function of the set $A$ and ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}$ denotes the indicator function of the complement of $A.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q) & =1-{1}_{A}(q) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(q)=1,$ we conclude that $q$ belongs to $\\overset{―}{A}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048808 :topic/id #uuid "c1647abf-57b4-5851-a828-2952c6947148" :topic/math-academy-id 948 :topic/title "Indicator Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9166a2cd-e482-5ef6-8dd0-7069988d19be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453592} {:answer/id #uuid "b1393175-0d07-53d3-844c-d6ae5f6863e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1393175-0d07-53d3-844c-d6ae5f6863e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453593} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef2fa57c-2909-5935-8d3c-0c6741e819f1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d018f001-d7c1-5d5f-ad00-a185cb6d375f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453594} {:answer/id #uuid "46f21955-ef1a-5e2c-8cda-63a6ce3b6b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d018f001-d7c1-5d5f-ad00-a185cb6d375f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453594} :answer-field/id #uuid "459b35ad-69a1-5c21-8aec-11bb813a98f2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f942421-ed53-502c-8912-7b5ca533e6d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453596} {:answer/id #uuid "eb24302b-1253-5c54-afa0-b4ff91533d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb24302b-1253-5c54-afa0-b4ff91533d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453597} :answer-field/id #uuid "4231e57f-0807-5822-9404-6d3a419c5c18" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c60efa7-9f70-50c9-8725-0334784ed791" :question/math-academy-id "q-174402" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(t)=1,\\,{1}_{B}(t)=1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t)=0$\n\n- **III.** $t\\in A\\cup B$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(t),{1}_{B}(t)\\} \\\\  & =max\\{1,1\\} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(t)=1,$ we conclude that $t$ belongs to $A\\cup B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048808 :topic/id #uuid "c1647abf-57b4-5851-a828-2952c6947148" :topic/math-academy-id 948 :topic/title "Indicator Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b4cfbc8-2b8c-5140-a8bb-7f6216d1c21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453586} {:answer/id #uuid "07d45975-75ad-5ac0-80a2-a67332372a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07d45975-75ad-5ac0-80a2-a67332372a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453587} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5ce266-0ba2-521f-8f38-84d3b53bb633" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa7035d2-94ee-5d7e-baff-b2c5f0b47416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453588} {:answer/id #uuid "895992ac-82c6-5750-b799-5234f11d0dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa7035d2-94ee-5d7e-baff-b2c5f0b47416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453588} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b53eb93-6623-55ce-83f0-193479b58d99" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a494fefa-d26c-53e8-af8a-a80ac83e1e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453590} {:answer/id #uuid "d42dfa9a-5b0a-598e-8bbc-e5091eaeb0f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d42dfa9a-5b0a-598e-8bbc-e5091eaeb0f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453591} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c89c5b6-f3d8-532d-9821-eeff63e9eb5a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "92b8a61e-f7a9-5e1e-adba-90e2fa6c6243" :question/math-academy-id "q-174394" :question/problem "$$\n{1}_{A}(-1)=1,\\,{1}_{B}(-1)=1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=0$\n\n- **III.** $-1\\in A\\cap B$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(-1),{1}_{B}(-1)\\} \\\\  & =min\\{1,1\\} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(-1)=1,$ we conclude that $-1$ belongs to $A\\cap B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd399539-33cf-5738-b970-fcc6c1d919c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using Properties of Indicator Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048808 :topic/id #uuid "c1647abf-57b4-5851-a828-2952c6947148" :topic/math-academy-id 948 :topic/title "Indicator Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271bd1b2-64d9-5cc7-bbec-b86ba10fc804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453568} {:answer/id #uuid "dae1f367-953f-5742-b452-749306fe9d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dae1f367-953f-5742-b452-749306fe9d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453569} :answer-field/id #uuid "95b271cf-9516-5e1c-8b28-1c9dbd8c9f68" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d4e5d4-6830-560c-878d-348a97dfcf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453570} {:answer/id #uuid "3d8118bf-d1fb-552a-a385-b0e89891b90a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05d4e5d4-6830-560c-878d-348a97dfcf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453570} :answer-field/id #uuid "0189df02-b3e6-5072-80bc-52efb3c878fc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9329cfe9-e21e-5113-b79d-99313f7bb970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453572} {:answer/id #uuid "d680e758-2e50-5500-9ac7-2a9c9e252fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d680e758-2e50-5500-9ac7-2a9c9e252fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453573} :answer-field/id #uuid "6302a2ae-7699-51e6-afdc-d665c6513e54" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a05322-998a-5d01-8b89-68a8bc93dd0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-174380" :question/problem "Given that ${1}_{A}(0)=0,$ which of the following statements about $\\overset{―}{A}$ are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=1$\n\n- **II.** ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=0$\n\n- **III.** $0\\in \\overset{―}{A}$\n\n*Hint: ${1}_{A}$ denotes the indicator function of the set $A$ and ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}$ denotes the indicator function of the complement of $A.$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the indicator functions of $\\overset{―}{A},$ $A\\cap B,$ and $A\\cup B$ have the following properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(x) & =1-{1}_{A}(x) \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cap \\,B}\\,(x) & =min\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\} \\\\ {1}_{A\\,\\cup \\,B}\\,(x) & =max\\{{1}_{A}(x),{1}_{B}(x)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0) & =1-{1}_{A}(0) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${1}_{\\overset{―}{A}}\\,(0)=1,$ we conclude that $0$ belongs to $\\overset{―}{A}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ad9700-5aaa-5b00-8d2f-acce6ed59c9a" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051069 :topic/id #uuid "7e5753ab-fcea-5d2f-ac49-4b475153e05c" :topic/math-academy-id 3027 :topic/title "Into Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccbbfd1c-6a08-5dc0-ae78-4e44e801c525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454084} {:answer/id #uuid "4a04030c-b721-5bf3-be03-2ecb5763411f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccbbfd1c-6a08-5dc0-ae78-4e44e801c525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454084} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ef9254a-d85b-51ec-9bb3-1270c8e3b239" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454792} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a872d88-d4b7-519b-807e-1141297b7849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454086} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd8f61b-4e41-5b3f-9d99-08b8822233ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdd8f61b-4e41-5b3f-9d99-08b8822233ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454087} :answer-field/id #uuid "accd4fd1-1699-5f0d-895e-42caceb1cf69" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "300e70b0-e346-5a85-b265-dcd48829a1f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454088} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e966b5-2ff2-5233-acc6-ce4cf8c0ff68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0e966b5-2ff2-5233-acc6-ce4cf8c0ff68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454089} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a2a2f00-559b-589b-b61f-d44d5d05df46" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a60aead-59e2-5a19-8c88-b84da12bb8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-90823" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=2-{x}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $(-\\infty ,-2]$\n\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,2],$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\n- **III.** $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/35/3575afe4fd4e5aa6754496154986b272a43fb5c035ec8d69621d52fad16ee1ea.png)\n\nRecall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph, the highest $y$-value is $2,$ and it occurs at the point $(0,2).$ The graph will cover all $y$-values lower than $y=2$, including $y=2$ itself. So the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,2].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,2]$, then for all $y$ contained within $(-\\infty ,2],$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=3\\in R.$ So, $f$ maps $R$ *into* $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161920 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa86a7e-d5b2-518a-8c43-8e6136bcf900" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051069 :topic/id #uuid "7e5753ab-fcea-5d2f-ac49-4b475153e05c" :topic/math-academy-id 3027 :topic/title "Into Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8ea4da6-07e1-57b7-a83b-7aaa01037d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472472} {:answer/id #uuid "4b72b35d-e95a-594a-9f80-c223cf007810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8ea4da6-07e1-57b7-a83b-7aaa01037d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :a