d "1346b272-ab34-50a3-8e2c-0cbfe3ad7ce0" :question/math-academy-id "q-105231" :question/problem "![](images/37/373448202bfd022f5629219b2c176f4096e4eeae275c1095798d77be92122cc2.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nI. $f(1)=4$\n\nII. $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y$\n\nIII. The function $f:X\\to Y$ is **into**\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. There is an arrow from $1\\in X$ to $2\\in Y.$ So, $f(1)=2\\ne 4.$\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the diagram, $4\\in Y$ has no preimage in $X$ because we have no arrows from $X$ to $4\\in Y.$ As a result, there exists some $y$ (i.e., $y=4$) contained within $Y$ such that $f(x)\\ne y$ for any $x$ in $X.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, $f$ is an *into* function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd378899-03ff-57a0-848c-11b93c8e5055" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is a Real Interval" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051069 :topic/id #uuid "7e5753ab-fcea-5d2f-ac49-4b475153e05c" :topic/math-academy-id 3027 :topic/title "Into Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42c7a1d5-2624-5583-aeae-da6b722a9800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473548} {:answer/id #uuid "d811fc76-0af3-5686-b258-9ec94ee426b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42c7a1d5-2624-5583-aeae-da6b722a9800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473548} :answer-field/id #uuid "63bfbf6e-2545-5f52-9799-41c7bca12360" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81660a94-f669-50bb-b01a-01293ad51c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473550} {:answer/id #uuid "51f4519c-df1c-5ed7-887b-6f1eca40896e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81660a94-f669-50bb-b01a-01293ad51c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473550} :answer-field/id #uuid "30d06d02-6bed-5ad7-8f32-70dcdb1c3125" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f56e9ea-8cf4-54d7-8527-7f8faf227ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473552} {:answer/id #uuid "4a669770-c352-5a86-88f4-78cbb1e23d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a669770-c352-5a86-88f4-78cbb1e23d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473553} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d9581ab-c4fe-5bba-9e72-95a487a5dfad" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2021b7c7-5d84-5929-874c-8d6923b11db1" :question/math-academy-id "q-90878" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are **into** functions?\n\nI. $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{3}$\n\nII. $g:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)$\n\nIII. $h:R\\to [0,\\infty )$ defined by $h(x)={e}^{x}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- I is a *not* an into function. Given any  $y\\in R,$ we can choose $x=\\sqrt[3]{y}\\in R.$ Then $f(x)=f(\\sqrt[3]{y})=(\\sqrt{y})^{3}=y.$\n\n- II is a *not* an into function. Given any  $y\\in R,$ we can choose $x={e}^{y}\\in R.$ Then $g(x)=g({e}^{y})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y})=y.$\n\n- III is an into function. Let's take $0\\in [0,\\infty ).$ There is no number $x\\in R$ such that $h(x)={e}^{x}=0.$ In fact, ${e}^{x}>0$ for all $x\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161921 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ad9700-5aaa-5b00-8d2f-acce6ed59c9a" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051069 :topic/id #uuid "7e5753ab-fcea-5d2f-ac49-4b475153e05c" :topic/math-academy-id 3027 :topic/title "Into Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "015d78ce-10e6-5aa2-8e40-5fcea0882254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453168} {:answer/id #uuid "00556d4d-0185-5264-9f2a-aa2a6f260ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "015d78ce-10e6-5aa2-8e40-5fcea0882254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453168} :answer-field/id #uuid "d74da5de-c05b-5fd4-ab1e-e42243e3aba7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e0f6634-264d-54c2-8e61-ed2f2e5776a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453170} {:answer/id #uuid "daa3ffd2-014c-5bfb-8d81-f8a7e9466f48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e0f6634-264d-54c2-8e61-ed2f2e5776a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453170} :answer-field/id #uuid "83459419-3597-52d7-9759-0b3f9e59c3aa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef48bf4-b61d-5d18-8d06-67153f8f0864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453172} {:answer/id #uuid "aead6e6b-ab86-52e2-ab5e-8e74bd9b4b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aead6e6b-ab86-52e2-ab5e-8e74bd9b4b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453173} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c719c4e-9fc3-558a-a32d-6604969ef25f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39b57e8a-5e0f-5758-8d6b-0d9667e7e35b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105258" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={2}^{-x}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of $f$ is $[0,\\infty )$\n\n- **II.** $∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\n- **III.** $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/c7/c79c1123036c978c8c4da514651c0bb1c8e3df34c8bbaff099bee601d568ed10.png)\n\nRecall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The graph will cover all $y$-values greater than $y=0$, excluding $y=0$ itself. So the range of the function is $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is false. Take, for example, $y=-1.$ Since the range of the function is $(0,\\infty ),$ there can't be an $x\\in R$ whose image is $-1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the function is not a surjection.  So, $f$ maps $R$ *into* $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd378899-03ff-57a0-848c-11b93c8e5055" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is a Real Interval" :topic/_knowle