ef 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8dd54609-ae0c-53a9-a2a1-7823f9aa6595" :question/math-academy-id "q-84747" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n- **I.** The number of times \"head\" is obtained when a coin is tossed $10$ times\n- **II.** The number of students in a class\n- **III.** The number of tickets sold for a concert in $3$ days\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of \"heads\" in $10$ tosses can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $10$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of students in a class cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\n- Random variable III could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of tickets sold for a concert cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105827 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "162690db-70b3-54a8-a920-576a484a42d9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Binomial Distribution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049632 :topic/id #uuid "06f86dee-da2a-593c-8633-10b2e3189b5c" :topic/math-academy-id 1395 :topic/title "Modeling With the Binomial Distribution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9dd05cc-1bdb-5141-b063-9c92310da718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472652} {:answer/id #uuid "94f08a3f-89c0-5762-a545-859a0f138cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94f08a3f-89c0-5762-a545-859a0f138cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472653} :answer-field/id #uuid "60b7a4a5-d299-5c0a-93b3-71d3f35b347c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd9fac83-8f9c-5590-8209-b3d493c3318e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472654} {:answer/id #uuid "e620d4f1-7625-5296-b0a1-f21ce51413f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd9fac83-8f9c-5590-8209-b3d493c3318e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472654} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c60bd00-8be9-5ef3-a107-4d31f9dcfa16" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c54a1e2-357b-527c-8373-a2a29e7c08be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472656} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6ad439-af82-5223-96a3-b2e1b7a0bf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f6ad439-af82-5223-96a3-b2e1b7a0bf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472657} :answer-field/id #uuid "14ef9316-2d4c-526c-baec-1f799427372f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e06f09da-f1cd-5f64-925a-f4c6e513e373" :question/math-academy-id "q-130361" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n- **I.** The number of trees in a forest of $300$ trees that have bird's nests\n- **II.** The number of vaccines administered in a country during one season\n- **III.** The number of odd numbers obtained when rolling an eight-sided die $10$ times\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of trees that have bird's nests among $300$ trees can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $300$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable II could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. Although receiving a vaccine can be interpreted as a \"success,\" there is not a fixed number of trials in this experiment.\n\n- Random variable III could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of odd numbers obtained when rolling an eight-sided die $10$ times can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $10$ independent experiments.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124615 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f2f4f4-af4a-597d-b6c6-afb82e708fc2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Steady-State Vectors of Stochastic Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048393 :topic/id #uuid "9babae1d-ca0d-5438-a2e4-a65dbba9f7ef" :topic/math-academy-id 1913 :topic/title "Steady-State Vectors"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16370931-5fc9-5536-9fd7-45afe61a10b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472688} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab6d543-ae19-5030-b18a-58051110b60a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ab6d543-ae19-5030-b18a-58051110b60a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472689} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4b12e7-31db-52dd-a206-759d60508923" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473739} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71dd4b86-fcee-58b2-a783-19a83e01d1dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472690} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7a9115-7513-51f1-a218-6359bc259d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71dd4b86-fcee-58b2-a783-19a83e01d1dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472690} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dc16e75-61f9-56a2-8f15-331022147565" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3605e075-25c5-54da-bf16-7e2307304916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472692} {:answer/id #uuid "9db4a1e3-8985-5443-8d1e-4853b29ea3d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3605e075-25c5-54da-bf16-7e2307304916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472692} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb71628d-05cf-5ce1-8a2b-c44a3882f058" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62944003-1237-5928-b405-2159dbe448f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-135308" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 & 0.8 \\\\ 0.7 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix},\\,q=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 \\\\ 0.9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- **II.** $Pq=q$\n- **III.** $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nPq=\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 & 0.8 \\\\ 0.7 & 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 \\\\ 0.9\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.03+0.72 \\\\ 0.07+0.18\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.75 \\\\ 0.25\\end{bmatrix}\\ne q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $Pq\\ne q,$ it is not a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048393 :topic/id #uuid "9babae1d-ca0d-5438-a2e4-a65dbba9f7ef" :topic/math-academy-id 1913 :topic/title "Steady-State Vectors"} :activity/title "Steady-State Vectors" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411596} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411620}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff71f3f5-8383-5815-ba42-289f14e16b57" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordered Pairs Belonging to a Standard Relation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050176 :topic/id #uuid "340a9570-0274-5535-83f9-7912961ba2ff" :topic/math-academy-id 4826 :topic/title "Relations on Infinite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7252f882-e1d0-5f4c-97ae-178f26c429a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453682} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e6f041-b9c8-5dec-9c77-5d180a2045a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7252f882-e1d0-5f4c-97ae-178f26c429a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453682} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0fb9cf8-d564-539e-805d-52f7a00587c6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454591} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cc0eeb2-bd34-5138-942f-42fd25bbc789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453684} {:answer/id #uuid "0fd5ada9-488b-5dcd-b4d1-014ba96151fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fd5ada9-488b-5dcd-b4d1-014ba96151fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453685} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c0bd65b-d5f3-556a-9229-07db49e7fafd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b5358be-8415-5ad4-ad47-03138a3beabd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453686} {:answer/id #uuid "b7fb7327-68b2-5f8c-ad61-022df27ddad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b5358be-8415-5ad4-ad47-03138a3beabd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453686} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ef3334-aefa-55ba-981a-899122d87488" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "579647d8-78b0-511b-8a94-882ec6fc1b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-212923" :question/problem "Given the relation $R$ on $N$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x>y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $6\\,R\\,8$\n\n- **II.** $7\\,R\\,2$\n\n- **III.** $9\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,1$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x>y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $>$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $≯$ (or, equivalently, $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $\\le $) are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $6>8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $7>2,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $\\le ,$ we have $9\\le 1,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff71f3f5-8383-5815-ba42-289f14e16b57" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordered Pairs Belonging to a Standard Relation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050176 :topic/id #uuid "340a9570-0274-5535-83f9-7912961ba2ff" :topic/math-academy-id 4826 :topic/title "Relations on Infinite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8587e734-006d-527c-a8c8-73090b97f285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453688} {:answer/id #uuid "982f7ef5-cc7e-5bf7-b407-84e014e93125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8587e734-006d-527c-a8c8-73090b97f285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453688} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d106978-3825-5783-b82f-260e5e09a3b0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e259bb54-f7de-5f20-98e7-eb69df3da9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453690} {:answer/id #uuid "875ac699-118d-533e-b443-208590e44f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e259bb54-f7de-5f20-98e7-eb69df3da9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453690} :answer-field/id #uuid "3afd2430-2118-5392-b5f4-b679fd87253d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454595} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f51b0a65-f7e4-568e-89be-e3f7bb38c80c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453692} {:answer/id #uuid "fc36dd43-c708-5750-9ae9-ccf65e36644d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc36dd43-c708-5750-9ae9-ccf65e36644d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453693} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec8cb5f-e291-5762-af3e-74fccda3b99e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8c98d98-74bc-5116-9f06-75c38fdcf981" :question/math-academy-id "q-212926" :question/problem "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∣y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $6\\,R\\,3$\n\n- **II.** $5\\,R\\,8$\n\n- **III.** $7\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,9$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $∣$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $∤$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $6∣3,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $5∣8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $∤,$ we have $7∤9,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203900 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d05194c-249d-54fb-91f1-f614c0f5e584" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordered Pairs Belonging to a Non-Standard Relation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050176 :topic/id #uuid "340a9570-0274-5535-83f9-7912961ba2ff" :topic/math-academy-id 4826 :topic/title "Relations on Infinite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3be0482-1c32-56e5-b32c-2635eff5a37b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453694} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0e7071-7690-5bc0-ab58-bae0b887668b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef0e7071-7690-5bc0-ab58-bae0b887668b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453695} :answer-field/id #uuid "910ed7f6-3d15-5d27-b480-93608abd7075" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454597} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0913762f-fc0f-5198-926a-6361a944a14e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453696} {:answer/id #uuid "8bec21ae-64f9-5251-8628-9b76f8b449b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bec21ae-64f9-5251-8628-9b76f8b449b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453697} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6814b33-9263-5cde-8a29-2d9f13981261" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454598} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdff64e7-785c-5a19-9710-d19ab6a540d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453698} {:answer/id #uuid "75097d40-93bc-5fc9-9154-d423738c8e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75097d40-93bc-5fc9-9154-d423738c8e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453699} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e55a813-df68-5a59-b03e-aaafd1e0f4b6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454599}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5b2a52b-fd77-5422-b1dc-3a9ca690060e" :question/math-academy-id "q-212983" :question/problem "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $0\\,R\\,2$\n\n- **II.** $1\\,R\\,9$\n\n- **III.** $4\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,13$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ or equivalently, $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $6∣(x-y-4).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. In this case, we have $6∣(0-2-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $6∣(1-9-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, we have $6∤(4-13-4),$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162013 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c67d532-acd9-5231-a27f-d39084863e01" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Spectral Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049849 :topic/id #uuid "1887f465-a1b8-5370-82f6-80e02b9d153a" :topic/math-academy-id 3120 :topic/title "The Spectral Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "577c6459-a68e-5617-9007-38fe998472ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454202} {:answer/id #uuid "9803254f-68b7-5b7e-936e-f2b01fcb4624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "577c6459-a68e-5617-9007-38fe998472ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454202} :answer-field/id #uuid "40924b97-51ec-57fe-9300-e75dc6817c4c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6225d8-02a3-5861-9a49-a929038a7ee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454204} {:answer/id #uuid "b251d743-a66c-5bae-a8cf-5ca14a90f254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d6225d8-02a3-5861-9a49-a929038a7ee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454204} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cae005c-ab57-5373-a6f8-1aefd15ba7ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454852} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7230c31-5927-5a08-a14e-0066312e17b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454206} {:answer/id #uuid "98cbb68b-2336-539d-bb6a-8b6710f91c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98cbb68b-2336-539d-bb6a-8b6710f91c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454207} :answer-field/id #uuid "e249821b-901a-5fb1-b815-d0984e6c7c99" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "409399cd-9cd7-53bb-83f5-ffa99003572c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95407" :question/problem "Given that $A$ is a real symmetric matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ must have a complex eigenvalue\n\n- **II.** $A$ is not diagonalizable\n\n- **III.** If $u$ and $v$ are two eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues, then $u⊥v$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $A$ is an $n\\times n$ symmetric matrix over $R$, the spectral theorem states the following:\n\n- The eigenvalues of $A$ are all real.\n\n- Eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues are orthogonal.\n\n- The dimension of the eigenspace for each eigenvalue equals the multiplicity of that eigenvalue as a root of the characteristic polynomial.\n\n- $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the spectral theorem, the eigenvalues are real.\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the spectral theorem, any symmetric matrix with real entries is orthogonally diagonalizable, so, $A$ is diagonalizable.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, eigenvectors corresponding to different eigenvalues must be orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/title "Mathematical Methods for the Physical Sciences II: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420497} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420512} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049849 :topic/id #uuid "1887f465-a1b8-5370-82f6-80e02b9d153a" :topic/math-academy-id 3120 :topic/title "The Spectral Theorem"} :activity/title "The Spectral Theorem" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559000} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559976}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4a5d6b1-e76a-5b33-8973-04d1d9062dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Orthogonality of a Two-Vector Set" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050910 :topic/id #uuid "708a8959-ec54-51e9-bf31-27b3539bdb74" :topic/math-academy-id 4319 :topic/title "Orthogonal Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8e2907-6f9f-5945-87a4-4b320b3c5c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472784} {:answer/id #uuid "363acb19-a7c4-58f9-889f-e407b2331d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f8e2907-6f9f-5945-87a4-4b320b3c5c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472784} :answer-field/id #uuid "51607494-5a75-5d4c-92f2-cb8a34490a90" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30463986-efbd-51fd-a6e9-b681bf1c31ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472786} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0850f2-9a46-5214-af3b-d2ee5b9d05f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30463986-efbd-51fd-a6e9-b681bf1c31ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472786} :answer-field/id #uuid "576b8513-a337-57bb-a0b8-42a8d11e9c97" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473788} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2da457c8-29f9-53a4-9a7b-82bd8117f5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472788} {:answer/id #uuid "9252ae02-4d55-5e0b-ab06-d7222907f63c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2da457c8-29f9-53a4-9a7b-82bd8117f5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472788} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8436333-b398-5406-b728-7406ac2b71f3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d807e12-6960-57f6-b74d-aa3fe66f0f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-178271" :question/problem "$$\n{u}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{u}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0$\n\nII. $\\{Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2}),Q({u}_{3})\\}$ is orthogonal\n\nIII. $\\{Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2}),Q({u}_{3})\\}$ is orthonormal\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false since\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=3\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that, for example, $Q({u}_{1})⊥̸Q({u}_{3})$ since\n\n$$\nQ({u}_{1})\\cdot Q({u}_{3})={u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false since the set is not even orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/title "Mathematical Methods for the Physical Sciences II: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420497} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420522} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/title "Mathematical Methods for the Physical Sciences II: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545198} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546007}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28cc783d-0e04-52b2-86df-236d896481c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473356} {:answer/id #uuid "46a9d129-ef86-55ea-a49c-ad5f819bc93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28cc783d-0e04-52b2-86df-236d896481c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473356} :answer-field/id #uuid "3759d021-c15d-5f94-bf0f-aa713cb06b19" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a3997f5-e7eb-5b23-a96c-7b63dc3096d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473358} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3abe6b-0a1b-5b0e-88aa-5350d602ba73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc3abe6b-0a1b-5b0e-88aa-5350d602ba73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473359} :answer-field/id #uuid "893f8dbf-f063-518c-9f05-3f90f1e69ab0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef8546b-c47c-5327-b7a1-c64d2e6e8c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473360} {:answer/id #uuid "4219ddb4-e932-5bd3-ae3b-efec94587db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ef8546b-c47c-5327-b7a1-c64d2e6e8c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473360} :answer-field/id #uuid "69938d67-9d92-50b1-a0c1-f38ae0ed687a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40dd9397-7325-5b4d-9df5-fd6f72af0a3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76978" :question/problem "Given that $7≡19\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=5$\n- **II.** $n=6$\n- **III.** $n=7$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=7-19=-12.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $5∤(-12).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=5.$\n\n- Note that $6∣(-12)$ because $(-12)÷6=-2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=6.$\n\n- Note that $7∤(-12).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"} :activity/title "Modular Congruence" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411972} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412012}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bae15cd1-2153-5765-8851-e11f5084cb94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472460} {:answer/id #uuid "b1941e2a-6399-5867-8fd2-8397a65c3736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1941e2a-6399-5867-8fd2-8397a65c3736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472461} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bd2169e-2963-565f-b2c3-acf4b032dd7d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473625} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3b3e9a3-10df-59d2-9aaf-723f387bfeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472462} {:answer/id #uuid "fda30b1a-11fa-50d8-acc0-9459616edd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda30b1a-11fa-50d8-acc0-9459616edd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472463} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3c7a717-d8a9-5f11-874c-25dd59863722" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473626} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3c377ae-6819-55aa-9670-acd2f63f98b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472464} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd132f0-8e79-5cac-a8ae-b44c9aeb8654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3c377ae-6819-55aa-9670-acd2f63f98b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472464} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab28e49-bde5-57c6-bbd6-efe09ce734f0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e4ac9e6-575d-537d-b731-f3556414b8f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-103492" :question/problem "Given that $15≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$, which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=2$\n- **II.** $n=4$\n- **III.** $n=6$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=15-7=8.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $2∣8$ because $8÷2=4,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\n- Note that $4∣8$ because $8÷4=2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=4.$\n\n- Note that $6∤8.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"} :activity/title "Modular Congruence" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411972} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412011}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcda3a9f-e8ac-5506-9e81-4e0c7adb449f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472862} {:answer/id #uuid "d51a1602-8985-583c-a7de-3b29ff3d2fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17