e/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd2ee89b-0850-5297-a810-7e54facce40b" :question/math-academy-id "q-212522" :question/problem "Given that $-7≡-3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n- **I.** $n=2$\n- **II.** $n=3$\n- **III.** $n=7$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=-7-(-3)=-4.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $2∣(-4)$ because $(-4)÷2=-2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\n- Note that $3∤(-4).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=3.$\n\n- Note that $7∤(-4).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049004 :topic/id #uuid "d28e701c-f952-587a-ba2a-6c1d3807d35a" :topic/math-academy-id 2641 :topic/title "Modular Congruence"} :activity/title "Modular Congruence" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411972} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412009}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6a3d254-c96f-5aa0-9db6-a587eb7cb2de" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Expression Involving Given Determinants and Matrix Types" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049159 :topic/id #uuid "df2bac79-2def-521c-b3f0-baba942d57fa" :topic/math-academy-id 1771 :topic/title "Basic Properties of Determinants"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3992319-c3cb-5cd7-aacc-a323343357a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473136} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbddcbd-2bf5-5bf2-97da-7ac2cb579d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bbddcbd-2bf5-5bf2-97da-7ac2cb579d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473137} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdf25248-1682-59e7-95bb-1d361adf535a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c0376ef-55b1-5b59-b083-c9871e0d3de3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473138} {:answer/id #uuid "1c79da45-cd4c-5734-b84e-b0bd3128fb29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c79da45-cd4c-5734-b84e-b0bd3128fb29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473139} :answer-field/id #uuid "d551a1fd-027b-537b-97dc-dacedd3d1459" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473964} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ce1514-9241-5a99-9a0c-8b77acadae75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473140} {:answer/id #uuid "99ad0e7f-4641-5c69-9b59-23ddd75d5e3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15ce1514-9241-5a99-9a0c-8b77acadae75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473140} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecef3e14-be54-5f11-801f-ad8edf3590fd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "03fcc7d2-8c99-53e1-b5b5-d7a0f5cd296f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42481" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=14$, and $I$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}(3I)=-13$\n\n- **II.** $-\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}(I)=-13$\n\n- **III.** $\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=-28$" :question/worked-solution "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})=\\text{det}(A)=14\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ndet(I)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3I & =3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a diagonal matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & ={3}^{3}=27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}(3I)=14-27=-13\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n-\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}(I)=-14+1=-13\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=14-14=0\\ne -28\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049159 :topic/id #uuid "df2bac79-2def-521c-b3f0-baba942d57fa" :topic/math-academy-id 1771 :topic/title "Basic Properties of Determinants"} :activity/title "Basic Properties of Determinants" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412054} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412066}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050906 :topic/id #uuid "70425962-eba3-5483-950c-6e00e8bba0c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1730 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of 2x2 Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "538e7fe6-b399-5899-a9f8-ecf6b1aae817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453842} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9fecf5-e15f-5c9e-8512-53b3ec9864c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef9fecf5-e15f-5c9e-8512-53b3ec9864c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453843} :answer-field/id #uuid "b361575c-aa03-5dbf-b411-97171b912788" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98ef04fa-1c1c-50a2-bdbb-2d85ae96f31e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453844} {:answer/id #uuid "48b4ae45-27c7-56eb-8ab2-ae845aa073be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98ef04fa-1c1c-50a2-bdbb-2d85ae96f31e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453844} :answer-field/id #uuid "93942ac4-88b5-56a0-89a7-6a3ffa4986b0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c36e8ab9-e979-5531-8a73-b3a76c58382b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453846} {:answer/id #uuid "145e9b16-dc59-5418-ac2c-92a5cf27033b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c36e8ab9-e979-5531-8a73-b3a76c58382b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453846} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c5d49d8-f8a3-5b1d-98ea-81d7fa4820c6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "79c14c2f-568d-5ff3-b628-6c8dd8d0639f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32169" :question/problem "Let \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The lines $5x-4y=0$ and $x+2y=0$ intersect at exactly one point\n- **II.** ${A}^{-1}$ does **not** exist\n- **III.** $Ax=0$ has no solution" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =14\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. \n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true by the fourth part of  the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95de2c3e-5810-5aa0-a1d0-b98b012572d4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Linearity Principle to the Solutions of a Homogeneous System of ODEs" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050221 :topic/id #uuid "3748163a-70f7-518f-9382-77b8230a6624" :topic/math-academy-id 3237 :topic/title "General Solutions of First-Order Linear Systems of ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1c0b90-23e9-5b83-a708-3ea2a44a1581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473040} {:answer/id #uuid "d96841dd-b0ce-57d2-8366-ed50689beb53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c1c0b90-23e9-5b83-a708-3ea2a44a1581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473040} :answer-field/id #uuid "334c6ac2-2b02-5e0f-a88a-b19789c7086c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473915} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43066d0d-a047-5a30-8822-f5d690da8c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473042} {:answer/id #uuid "12848657-20bc-5e4e-8323-c54bfc0aa80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43066d0d-a047-5a30-8822-f5d690da8c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473042} :answer-field/id #uuid "34af04fe-4273-5909-afb6-13e9d8b36c79" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473916} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "216b9e19-7285-56cb-8603-99b3f8d13d7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473044} {:answer/id #uuid "a0db2386-3a66-5f9c-a3fd-5640d25f6a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0db2386-3a66-5f9c-a3fd-5640d25f6a54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473045} :answer-field/id #uuid "381905b6-4e83-545a-8560-cb908ea74f55" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71a6807f-51a3-5e94-a65a-0087aa5dc119" :question/math-academy-id "q-330333" :question/problem "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)\\times {x}_{2}(t)$\n\n- **II.** $x(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$\n\n- **III.** $x(t)=-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$" :question/worked-solution "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier is not a constant.\n\n- Option III is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=0$ and ${c}_{2}=-3,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050597 :topic/id #uuid "574a92ea-12bd-55d4-a248-945298d922a1" :topic/math-academy-id 2655 :topic/title "Residue Classes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d90f90f5-3e74-572c-aa89-9724b4da180e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453988} {:answer/id #uuid "11a83033-f355-5373-a7f0-51d0ef965472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d90f90f5-3e74-572c-aa89-9724b4da180e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453988} :answer-field/id #uuid "69f93893-49bf-50eb-9cb8-5100bc1b0a48" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454744} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caafc5ae-8676-58f7-be01-e74b00b73515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453990} {:answer/id #uuid "2dad5cff-3cef-5b95-a702-f2684708b692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caafc5ae-8676-58f7-be01-e74b00b73515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453990} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf3b9fd7-6d29-582c-857b-0ed344345e75" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2ebe3c7-2898-5c09-95a0-a9683da87a51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453992} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf20969-d67c-5204-9e7c-1a8067b679d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cf20969-d67c-5204-9e7c-1a8067b679d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453993} :answer-field/id #uuid "471dce59-5681-5b77-b94e-7501e5f87b82" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f9012f2-83ba-5f6f-b553-2ea47d5d4f81" :question/math-academy-id "q-78640" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** There are $3$ distinct residue classes modulo $6$\n\n- **II.** $[5]_{3}\\cap [1]_{3}\\ne ∅$\n\n- **III.** $Z=[3]_{2}\\cup [6]_{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}=\\{[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}\\}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. There are exactly $6$ distinct residue classes modulo $6.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $5≢1\\,(\\text{mod }3),$ we have that $[5]_{3}\\cap [1]_{3}=∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[3]_{2} & =[1+2\\cdot 1]_{2}=[1]_{2} \\\\ [6]_{2} & =[0+2\\cdot 3]_{2}=[0]_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[3]_{2}\\cup [6]_{2} & =[1]_{2}\\cup [0]_{2} \\\\  & =[0]_{2}\\cup [1]_{2} \\\\  & =Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050597 :topic/id #uuid "574a92ea-12bd-55d4-a248-945298d922a1" :topic/math-academy-id 2655 :topic/title "Residue Classes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2c3ece1-9a5e-52f4-8699-73139d9a6a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473004} {:answer/id #uuid "0563223b-220c-58df-9201-b1e95a708764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0563223b-220c-58df-9201-b1e95a708764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473005} :answer-field/id #uuid "112786af-b7c6-53b8-bad3-b5ce3ac037cf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473897} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2beadd3e-28d3-5177-a991-6ac6e547dcd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473006} {:answer/id #uuid "05064f80-545d-5b21-ac39-0deff32cdce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2beadd3e-28d3-5177-a991-6ac6e547dcd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473006} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5d9f3bb-8e2c-5510-b22f-bc287c4c9d3d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae4c9241-2ba0-574d-b41a-55b7771a6440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473008} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc3c013-0913-5495-8e49-25ca6a801a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bc3c013-0913-5495-8e49-25ca6a801a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473009} :answer-field/id #uuid "6116a5f6-75a3-57f5-8b9a-87c19cf2e1cc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44e36839-2675-57c4-abf9-91a0b0717003" :question/math-academy-id "q-214450" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[4]_{7}?$\n\nI. $-3$\n\nII. $6$\n\nIII. $18$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[4]_{7}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $4$ modulo $7.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[4]_{7} & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=4+7k,\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{4+7k\\,|\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,\\,4-2\\cdot 7,\\,4-7,\\,4,\\,4+7,\\,4+2\\cdot 7,\\,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-10,-3,4,11,18,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-3$ and $18$ belong to $[4]_{7},$ while $6$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1fe7ea-d91e-5440-b756-37a460a18f19" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Residue Classes Containing a Given Element" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050597 :topic/id #uuid "574a92ea-12bd-55d4-a248-945298d922a1" :topic/math-academy-id 2655 :topic/title "Residue Classes"}]}] :question/answer-