d/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e91f8fe9-c6f2-558a-bf39-b0389019d5ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-86021" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[7]_{11}?$\n\nI. $18$\n\nII. $-4$\n\nIII. $15$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[7]_{11}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $7$ modulo $11.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[7]_{11} & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=7+11k,\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{7+11k\\,|\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,\\,7-2\\cdot 11,\\,7-11,\\,7,\\,7+11,\\,7+2\\cdot 11,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-15,-4,7,18,29,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-4$ and $18$ belong to $[7]_{11},$ while $15$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050597 :topic/id #uuid "574a92ea-12bd-55d4-a248-945298d922a1" :topic/math-academy-id 2655 :topic/title "Residue Classes"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99c866b5-fa78-5463-879f-91c030b81919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453994} {:answer/id #uuid "ed31939a-f058-5205-8c6b-722767e7b7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed31939a-f058-5205-8c6b-722767e7b7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 175921