/id #edb/ref 17592186453723} :answer-field/id #uuid "81dbaedc-783b-5b68-8134-849222d627b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "73a43b1a-0275-523e-ad37-d72b83b2b870" :question/math-academy-id "q-213296" :question/problem "Given that $10a≡10b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n\n- **II.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n\n- **III.** $5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10a & ≡10b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\ 2\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 3) \\\\ 5a & ≡5b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $gcd(5,3)=1,$ by the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement I and the first property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415046 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3822141e-3cea-5c34-b925-a522c2273335" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Division Properties" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050689 :topic/id #uuid "5f54d743-67b1-5023-a4c2-42de103b3b6d" :topic/math-academy-id 2675 :topic/title "The Division Properties of Modular Arithmetic"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f8df1f5-a326-5744-b94d-a8f8dbfaf3eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453736} {:answer/id #uuid "05e1a544-e990-505b-b4dd-5cf2c163f81e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f8df1f5-a326-5744-b94d-a8f8dbfaf3eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453736} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f272d94-f2e5-5bc4-8d99-cb3bdc0c9e77" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454618} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d291526-f242-5aee-bbee-15dca92f7c4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453738} {:answer/id #uuid "1f74de5b-6f10-546d-b300-bc3936015893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f74de5b-6f10-546d-b300-bc3936015893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453739} :answer-field/id #uuid "097f5b2b-3a82-5378-a95b-73c99e48f1df" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454619} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2da2bbfb-eaba-5993-9806-64aa68804c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/