true. By statement II and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,⟺\\,9a≡9b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152094 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca70f6c-d087-5b8e-aff2-581adca9ed1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the First Division Property" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050689 :topic/id #uuid "5f54d743-67b1-5023-a4c2-42de103b3b6d" :topic/math-academy-id 2675 :topic/title "The Division Properties of Modular Arithmetic"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "215a3373-c92b-5c76-a4aa-8454ff12465a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453102} {:answer/id #uuid "cdae0bbe-0548-5c6a-8e4c-2659c4b03746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "215a3373-c92b-5c76-a4aa-8454ff12465a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453102} :answer-field/id #uuid "b286f757-c4a9-549a-af99-b2c466dac029" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454301} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b19bd3d0-0305-5a5a-ae7c-5fd65541f397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453104} {:answer/id #uuid "55d60b87-ecc4-58bf-9ce9-8c13885c95b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55d60b87-ecc4-58bf-9ce9-8c13885c95b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453105} :answer-field/id #uuid "f935b726-d481-597f-9800-4e23100000cb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454302} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae166ede-2a92-5e22-a248-5406db0b0133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453106} {:answer/id #uuid "ee84c16f-325f-5ece-90ba-2114c5a76e05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae166ede-2a92-5e22-a248-5406db0b0133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453106} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfbb6054-d1be-5f93-a093-b2c8e849540a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4019e4a-38d9-5f9b-be44-5c0d23af5290" :question/math-academy-id "q-103171" :question/problem "Given that $2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n\n- **II.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n\n- **III.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWe're asked to consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\text{gcd}(2,8)=2.$\n\nApplying the division property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a & ≡2b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 2\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 4) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 4) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152096 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3822141e-3cea-5c34-b925-a522c2273335" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Division Properties" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050689 :topic/id #uuid "5f54d743-67b1-5023-a4c2-42de103b3b6d" :topic/math-academy-id 2675 :topic/title "The Division Properties of Modular Arithmetic"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "551f0b7d-81e5-5a0c-85ad-ee3443a9ac05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453730} {:answer/id #uuid "26c14664-1010-5406-a08a-c5f282d03a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26c14664-1010-5406-a08a-c5f282d03a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453731} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d627ec5-3122-5886-aba1-f7ca43ccab0a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454615} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47aab34d-d405-565c-b065-276e17d2ef29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453732} {:answer/id #uuid "dd687af5-136d-54a7-b6be-55f311c4b328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47aab34d-d405-565c-b065-276e17d2ef29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453732} :answer-field/id #uuid "404c6b13-338a-5bba-9714-6cf1dc4bf388" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454616} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2ea069e-68e9-5f34-8ba8-e9524f37e465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453734} {:answer/id #uuid "0078cc05-b102-5887-ab18-437410f29d26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0078cc05-b102-5887-ab18-437410f29d26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453735} :answer-field/id #uuid "605e7eae-f89a-5236-a71d-ea2132fe786a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca808cf3-f807-5d95-a81f-b5460b52df5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-213392" :question/problem "Given that $3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n\n- **II.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$\n\n- **III.** $4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a & ≡3b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,9) \\\\ 3\\cdot a & ≡3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{3}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{3}\\cdot 3) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement I and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f567e86-63a5-512d-b830-be97bedcf0c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Second Division Property" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050689 :topic/id #uuid "5f54d743-67b1-5023-a4c2-42de103b3b6d" :topic/math-academy-id 2675 :topic/title "The Division Properties of Modular Arithmetic"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e92c9d5b-f959-5953-90a6-a8ecdbf1b02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472436} {:answer/id #uuid "d095dde9-8464-578b-92bf-70c871371f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e92c9d5b-f959-5953-90a6-a8ecdbf1b02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472436} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8b01d97-65f0-5722-86fe-d4234d0c21d6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cdb196b-3c66-57d4-a771-2f16dffdb90b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472438} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b25acd-0ce3-5e8e-b537-d16fe94e9392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cdb196b-3c66-57d4-a771-2f16dffdb90b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472438} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bd839d3-3c71-56c5-b3bc-cbdfb0f3dfeb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23df32a4-4c9b-5ad1-a8ef-93ba58941242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472440} {:answer/id #uuid "18bc3fc6-b8ea-5101-a626-36ebabc05ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18bc3fc6-b8ea-5101-a626-36ebabc05ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472441} :answer-field/id #uuid "41ef972a-bbba-523c-82f9-fc664ae2cd7a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cdd37720-ffc4-552d-8b81-f3aa2f866efb" :question/math-academy-id "q-103026" :question/problem "If \n$ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$\nis equivalent to\n$a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$\nwhich of the following could be the value of $k?$\n\nI. $k=8$\n\nII. $k=-12$\n\nIII. $k=-15$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\n$$\n\nprovided that $k$ and $n$ are coprime. In other words, we require $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1.$\n\nIn this case, the modulus $n=8.$ Let's consider each value of $k$ in turn.\n\n- If $k=8,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(8,8)=8\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=8.$\n\n- If $k=-12,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(-12,8)=4\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=-12.$\n\n- If $k=-15,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(-15,8)=1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is valid for $k=-15.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152094 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca70f6c-d087-5b8e-aff2-581adca9ed1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the First Division Property" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050689 :topic/id #uuid "5f54d743-67b1-5023-a4c2-42de103b3b6d" :topic/math-academy-id 2675 :topic/title "The Division Properties of Modular Arithmetic"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82e89cf2-06e0-5398-8753-970f44e06da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453096} {:answer/id #uuid "e65928c6-1755-58d7-afe6-af81f2e18bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82e89cf2-06e0-5398-8753-970f44e06da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453096} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ee3331f-371c-59cf-8aea-4634363e0b0e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454298} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c37544a-78d9-5d1e-970f-c6e77d857e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453098} {:answer/id #uuid "b06a7d11-7b5e-5e92-92fc-c73ab108160b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b06a7d11-7b5e-5e92-92fc-c73ab108160b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453099} :answer-field/id #uuid "07fbac1d-135b-5cbb-8002-714d3bf0845c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454299} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b57a3b84-f9e4-52dd-8bbb-9a58dee94b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453100} {:answer/id #uuid "e40c642a-e2b4-5e2c-a7f0-d2023a84eb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b57a3b84-f9e4-52dd-8bbb-9a58dee94b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453100} :answer-field/id #uuid "2534715f-1d54-5a13-8947-b595d2367807" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d23e3ed0-5575-5880-b9bf-7ff1adfe9936" :question/math-academy-id "q-103168" :question/problem "Given that $3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n\n- **II.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n\n- **III.** $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWe're asked to consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12)\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\text{gcd}(3,12)=3.$\n\nApplying the division property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a & ≡3b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,12) \\\\ 3\\cdot a & ≡3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3\\cdot 4) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{3}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{3}\\cdot 4) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415053 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152095 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f567e86-63a5-512d-b830-be97bedcf0c8" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Second Division Property" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050689 :topic/id #uuid "5f54d743-67b1-5023-a4c2-42de103b3b6d" :topic/math-academy-id 2675 :topic/title "The Division Properties of Modular Arithmetic"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d5fee9c-8592-5941-94ba-f732ff2e2b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472430} {:answer/id #uuid "6e43f309-2046-5c4b-88b6-e63a40e10a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d5fee9c-8592-5941-94ba-f732ff2e2b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472430} :answer-field/id #uuid "08c83890-765e-5a1e-be4c-e431339df65e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473610} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82d50d77-6a1d-59f7-8987-baae4b552219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472432} {:answer/id #uuid "aa194468-2830-58df-af8c-0429fcc1e1c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa194468-2830-58df-af8c-0429fcc1e1c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472433} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebad9b6f-1dd8-5d82-a7aa-d843aa29a947" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26eda066-7454-5d62-bd57-ea93331cdf97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472434} {:answer/id #uuid "5a159447-da3a-5921-aca7-0f9c4d8484cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26eda066-7454-5d62-bd57-ea93331cdf97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472434} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a5d827b-cc7e-5f2d-af32-37ff6889a8bb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eaf9f361-8af6-5a67-abf5-86a0bbac7a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103018" :question/problem "If \n$ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$\nis equivalent to\n$a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10),$\nwhich of the following could be the value of $k?$\n\nI. $k=12$\n\nII. $k=3$\n\nIII. $k=-5$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\n$$\n\nprovided that $k$ and $n$ are coprime. In other words, we require $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1.$\n\nIn this case, the modulus $n=10.$ Let's consider each value of $k$ in turn.\n\n- If $k=12,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(12,10)=2\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=12.$\n\n- If $k=3,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(3,10)=1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is valid for $k=3.$\n\n- If $k=-5,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(-5,10)=5\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=-5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124485 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Given Set Is Linearly Independent Given Information on Its Elements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c31adaa2-aedb-51ee-98cc-f5a5cb7cb242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453874} {:answer/id #uuid "063facdd-b115-5116-95a9-caa5bdab8f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c31adaa2-aedb-51ee-98cc-f5a5cb7cb242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453874} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2096ae6-ffb1-5d8a-b2ca-ba762fb6d409" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3745e8da-fba3-5de6-8ee2-c06592f6933b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453876} {:answer/id #uuid "5f81960a-dd97-5893-98af-f4a31d1a3af6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f81960a-dd97-5893-98af-f4a31d1a3af6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453877} :answer-field/id #uuid "2316b283-b952-57f0-ab87-cfeeb442fa55" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890bce99-21fe-5928-b77c-8e07e141f72f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453878} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7aea04-d3e3-5812-868c-e15e8ab20d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "890bce99-21fe-5928-b77c-8e07e141f72f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453878} :answer-field/id #uuid "33daad36-10f5-52d9-b312-d81cb77a900b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0c07b7ca-2c8b-5a74-a857-c6a369e5fb28" :question/math-academy-id "q-35580" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly dependent and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$\n- **II.** ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$\n- **III.** ${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, solving equation ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ for ${v}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=-\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{3}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nMoreover, ${x}_{2}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nHence, ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent set, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3}+{x}_{3}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas no non-zero solution. Hence, ${v}_{4}$ is not a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415054} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415062} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048257 :topic/id #uuid "8cc35c33-61af-5ac3-971b-a33b8bbdcb9d" :topic/math-academy-id 1908 :topic/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces"} :activity/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420706} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420718}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4a5d6b1-e76a-5b33-8973-04d1d9062dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Orthogonality of a Two-Vector Set" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050910 :topic/id #uuid "708a8959-ec54-51e9-bf31-27b3539bdb74" :topic/math-academy-id 4319 :topic/title "Orthogonal Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d08864-6101-5251-8351-5c0043998d07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472778} {:answer/id #uuid "1a22dbe5-0d2b-5c0a-9531-8c54bafdc81e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a22dbe5-0d2b-5c0a-9531-8c54bafdc81e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472779} :answer-field/id #uuid "71e4259d-b2ae-5c52-927d-7cf47899f776" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c84ccb50-f1be-591e-8bac-35014caba949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472780} {:answer/id #uuid "19621db5-93e2-50ee-9ddb-8440f2d6f313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19621db5-93e2-50ee-9ddb-8440f2d6f313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472781} :answer-field/id #uuid "7af95f9f-6948-54ed-b3d3-37b3b7e7a68c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b309452-f7e7-54e9-bbdf-9a3025bd85c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472782} {:answer/id #uuid "f4968354-f03a-5157-9f0d-8be8dbd50643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b309452-f7e7-54e9-bbdf-9a3025bd85c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472782} :answer-field/id #uuid "46245871-924f-5edd-8bb1-a6c28bc755b4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a7fbace-2464-5d79-be05-e6f28745c3de" :question/math-academy-id "q-178014" :question/problem "$$\n{u}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$\n- **II.** ${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthogonal\n- **III.** ${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthonormal\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe linear transformation $Q$ being orthogonal is equivalent to the following:\n\n- The matrix $Q$ of transformation $Q$ relative to any orthonormal basis (including the standard basis) of ${R}^{n}$ is orthogonal.\n\n- $||Q(x)||=||x||.$\n\n- If $x⊥y$ then $Q(x)⊥Q(y)$ for any $x,y\\in {R}^{n}.$ In general, $Q$ preserves the angle between any two vectors.\n\n- $Q$ maps any orthogonal (orthonormal) set into an orthogonal (orthonormal) set.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=12-12=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $Q({u}_{1})⊥Q({u}_{2})$ since\n\n$$\nQ({u}_{1})\\cdot Q({u}_{2})={u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that, for example, $Q({u}_{1})$ is not a unit vector since\n\n$$\n‖Q({u}_{1})‖=‖{u}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050910 :topic/id #uuid "708a8959-ec54-51e9-bf31-27b3539bdb74" :topic/math-academy-id 4319 :topic/title "Orthogonal Linear Transformations"} :activity/title "Orthogonal Linear Transformations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415149} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415160}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048574 :topic/id #uuid "aad2999b-dacb-527f-a4a8-1fce51919fe6" :topic/math-academy-id 4257 :topic/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80e50955-37f8-51bc-83cc-cb950145c252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472820} {:answer/id #uuid "495a8b40-49df-5a56-9235-6ebb943146aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "495a8b40-49df-5a56-9235-6ebb943146aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472821} :answer-field/id #uuid "33d25ffd-2c6e-5b5b-99df-560a24530be3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1322f1f2-f4c5-54d8-87cc-355df640d02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472822} {:answer/id #uuid "33f4cad9-66cd-545d-9ac0-97d5414f12cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33f4cad9-66cd-545d-9ac0-97d5414f12cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472823} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aeb8409-1020-570b-8cec-0822b2e40889" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ff70513-8053-559e-b6b1-7a97e4aa128d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472824} {:answer/id #uuid "78ab4291-cd70-5529-b069-e726e0430998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ff70513-8053-559e-b6b1-7a97e4aa128d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472824} :answer-field/id #uuid "aebe7e6e-372c-5557-a0e2-e163a4bed7dd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d6a13d3-ad69-5578-b6a3-a3b3842749f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183354" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\ge 2.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $-x\\le -2.$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n- **I.** If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n- **II.** $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n- **III.** If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ or if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ if and only if $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- $x\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $-x\\le -2.$\n\n- If $x\\ge 2$ then $-x\\le -2,$ and if $-x\\le -2$ then $x\\ge 2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048574 :topic/id #uuid "aad2999b-dacb-527f-a4a8-1fce51919fe6" :topic/math-academy-id 4257 :topic/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates"} :activity/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415162} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415191} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048574 :topic/id #uuid "aad2999b-dacb-527f-a4a8-1fce51919fe6" :topic/math-academy-id 4257 :topic/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates"} :activity/title "Conditional Statements With Predicates" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499649} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500392}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049150 :topic/id #uuid "deab20e7-248d-57af-ad42-5509f60f2d31" :topic/math-academy-id 3360 :topic/title "Path Independence of Line Integrals"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59393bce-26a0-53f4-b9ee-a4b60e0309ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453336} {:answer/id #uuid "d3ec25f8-9101-5ec4-ae2b-1947b4fed11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3ec25f8-9101-5ec4-ae2b-1947b4fed11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453337} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aafa3ab-4c0c-5ec8-8508-509f0aa15d9e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454418} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59eb0512-2892-504c-817d-6e1c62f596b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453338} {:answer/id #uuid "8c2be482-8af1-5d7d-8d56-389be603fc9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c2be482-8af1-5d7d-8d56-389be603fc9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453339} :answer-field/id #uuid "359d2acf-2ea6-56b6-a467-a84c75cf4d9e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454419} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7762d99b-6748-51f0-9769-d7e020b910e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453340} {:answer/id #uuid "761205e9-2c61-502f-8e9d-e4e3f37407aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7762d99b-6748-51f0-9769-d7e020b910e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453340} :answer-field/id #uuid "95713f76-4916-53c2-b271-58871420022e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0027cfb5-d932-549f-8cc6-973642895e8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-125743" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F$ is conservative.\n\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=e,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2e-1,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\sqrt{x},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives exist and are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $F$ is conservative, there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$ Reconstructing the function $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})-f(0,0) \\\\  & ={e}^{1}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{e}^{0}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =e\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $F$ is conservative and ${C}_{2}$ has the same initial and terminal points as ${C}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=e.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049150 :topic/id #uuid "deab20e7-248d-57af-ad42-5509f60f2d31" :topic/math-academy-id 3360 :topic/title "Path Independence of Line Integrals"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e94047db-68c4-551f-9095-b7004ca8440d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453324} {:answer/id #uuid "bb26d5f6-a66c-5844-b1b4-09be8fba0088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb26d5f6-a66c-5844-b1b4-09be8fba0088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453325} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a92e66-5e63-57a1-a0c4-007b140902d2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454412} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90c212f9-6c73-5efa-827a-5c7e1827ff4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453326} {:answer/id #uuid "d032a76d-d4bb-5471-9f1d-f875814c51b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d032a76d-d4bb-5471-9f1d-f875814c51b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453327} :answer-field/id #uuid "7023734c-f76f-51a8-9faa-f0979cbea5ab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454413} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09069a3c-ed3c-50a5-9d67-301f8b9abc91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453328} {:answer/id #uuid "da2b872b-a120-58a1-8c06-6c98a0c03cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09069a3c-ed3c-50a5-9d67-301f8b9abc91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453328} :answer-field/id #uuid "7125f222-da47-5c32-9e27-3e728ad73ef9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41c787c2-8fe3-51ae-aef3-bfbcd04677ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-125720" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨y,\\,x⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(\\sqrt{2},2)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F$ is conservative.\n\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2\\sqrt{2},$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-\\sqrt{2},$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y={x}^{2},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives exist and are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $F$ is conservative, there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$ Reconstructing the function $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf=xy.\n$$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(\\sqrt{2},2)-f(0,0) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $F$ is conservative and ${C}_{2}$ has the same initial and terminal points as ${C}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049150 :topic/id #uuid "deab20e7-248d-57af-ad42-5509f60f2d31" :topic/math-academy-id 3360 :topic/title "Path Independence of Line Integrals"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d72dfe19-644e-58ac-b092-ca0bf0a32235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453330} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3cb706-2c7c-59c6-9797-8f2413c3c0ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d3cb706-2c7c-59c6-9797-8f2413c3c0ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453331} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa85dc7-977b-504c-9e63-6eaa9497ca86" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454415} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fc76864-a6b1-5bc1-9012-9c15cd8d9c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453332} {:answer/id #uuid "9de221a3-7ed0-563b-8bfe-b20e6e8988e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9de221a3-7ed0-563b-8bfe-b20e6e8988e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453333} :answer-field/id #uuid "6454a9c4-5959-5c99-9e74-da908dab25c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454416} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea26c04-19a4-5d02-95f7-713e29db1fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453334} {:answer/id #uuid "05e0a248-34b8-5d04-9e61-a958287d7eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fea26c04-19a4-5d02-95f7-713e29db1fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453334} :answer-field/id #uuid "771420e3-311e-5ce3-b340-03646c706117" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef46b0f0-6f4c-53dd-b0f1-5e1b301fe037" :question/math-academy-id "q-125736" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{y},\\,x{e}^{y}⟩$ and the points $A(1,0)$ and $B(3,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F$ is conservative.\n\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=8,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=3,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives exist and are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $F$ is conservative, there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$ Reconstructing the function $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf=x{e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(3,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-f(1,0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $F$ is conservative and ${C}_{2}$ has the same initial and terminal points as ${C}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773 :topic/id #uuid "659072cc-8b2c-5e8d-b6a6-88321581f47f" :topic/math-academy-id 3713 :topic/title "Circulation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55d9a389-0207-5627-8724-2ab06942a52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472532} {:answer/id #uuid "8021b753-e25f-51ff-8c8f-fab09d9d89b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8021b753-e25f-51ff-8c8f-fab09d9d89b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472533} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f990914-9c06-5321-9dbf-d829370622d6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f7147a8-f34e-5218-b7c5-8ea2c830c0bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472534} {:answer/id #uuid "308c82b6-5505-533c-a6a4-f3335f961206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "308c82b6-5505-533c-a6a4-f3335f961206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472535} :answer-field/id #uuid "be5dec92-40f9-56cc-a873-06f88cbc4087" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "975f0d9b-1723-5cdd-bb95-28c94959e5c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472536} {:answer/id #uuid "8caa6e88-f7bc-5579-83d6-8f86c7a5803f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975f0d9b-1723-5cdd-bb95-28c94959e5c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472536} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b8664d6-4e9d-52a7-ac0d-f153ff8d27fa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e8f010b-1d85-5f55-981d-5803f1cc03c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-125645" :question/problem "![](images/98/981d966645eec322afbfe28a5a1f519eeab8b3557692dcce368a87fe748dddd6.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/b2/b2473eb0c505d75d2c448c1a0d714d05d42737ce8d601401e925834a25ae9e14.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](images/85/8513d9d15d204b6f63f310a37465d6b8dfb21239ca412bac7d3b9936f2bf5ebf.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773 :topic/id #uuid "659072cc-8b2c-5e8d-b6a6-88321581f47f" :topic/math-academy-id 3713 :topic/title "Circulation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51baee7c-4f09-5886-aa36-1dcdf90f0b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472538} {:answer/id #uuid "46738186-25bf-5244-a8cd-2cfae05fe1b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51baee7c-4f09-5886-aa36-1dcdf90f0b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472538} :answer-field/id #uuid "2343f5a2-9a6f-5456-bd97-3e506bdd18a6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d8099c-d11a-55ed-bd66-5bc9bfad9a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472540} {:answer/id #uuid "91e139e0-9b3e-56d8-b8c4-b1714fe1291e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d8099c-d11a-55ed-bd66-5bc9bfad9a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472540} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7751525-7c16-596e-8c69-5d8f650009fe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "860e69b6-35d8-5d31-ba12-9202b482813d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472542} {:answer/id #uuid "4b8bf411-3432-5e8d-81ec-008c129f27d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8bf411-3432-5e8d-81ec-008c129f27d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472543} :answer-field/id #uuid "09f14689-536e-5986-8e63-f7f4a981a39f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77e87c43-f6db-5082-9277-93ef32960dff" :question/math-academy-id "q-125659" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡2y\\,i+\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{1+4{y}^{2}}\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $F$ is **not** conservative\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n- **III.** ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any ellipse $C\\in {R}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4x}{1+4{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}]
